-moduledoc """
TurboSHAKE128 (RFC 9861) is an extendable-output function (XOF) with
the same sponge and rate as SHAKE128 but using the Keccak-p[1600]
permutation reduced to 12 rounds, roughly doubling its speed. It
hashes an input of any length into an output of any requested length
and targets 128-bit security.

`init/0` and the one-shot function use the standard domain byte
`domain_standard/0` (`16#1F`). `init_with_domain/1` selects another
domain byte so that different uses of TurboSHAKE128 produce
independent outputs; RFC 9861 defines domain bytes from `16#01` to
`16#7F`.

The streaming functions thread an opaque `t:state/0` through `init/0`,
`update/2`, and `squeeze/2`. Every call returns a new state and leaves its
argument unchanged. Squeezing continues the output stream: consecutive
`squeeze/2` calls on the returned states produce the same bytes as one
longer squeeze, so output can be read incrementally. Updates over large
inputs yield to other processes between chunks.

```erlang
